---
status: 'published';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Guides - Imagine the structure. Choose the path."
  description="A good site is a clear doorway. Start with the outcome you want, then design the path that delivers it. Add depth when you are ready."
>
  <!-- Hero with background image (fixed stacking) -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <img
        src="/images/guides/night-sky-constellation.webp"
        alt=""
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-40 dark:opacity-50"
      />
      <div
        class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-white/80 via-white/50 to-white/10 dark:from-gray-950/85 dark:via-gray-950/70 dark:to-gray-950/40"
      >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative z-10">
      <div
        class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-24 md:py-32 text-center"
      >
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 mb-2"
        >
          Guides
        </p>
        <h1
          class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Imagine the structure. Choose the path.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          A good site is a clear doorway. Start with the outcome you want, then
          design the path that delivers it. Add depth when you are ready.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Content -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
      <!-- Section 1 - Start here -->
      <section id="start-here" class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 md:gap-10 items-start">
          <div>
            <h2
              class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
            >
              Start here: do you need a website right now?
            </h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-4">
              Not everyone needs a full site today. If your profiles and
              referrals already answer the basics, a single link may be enough.
              When questions repeat or trust depends on more than a profile, a
              simple site becomes the clearest door.
            </p>

            <div
              class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
            >
              <ul
                class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
              >
                <li>Not yet: referrals and profiles cover most needs.</li>
                <li>
                  Simple site: answer who it is for, what you do, and how to
                  start.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Go deeper: show thinking, outcomes, and distinct offers.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Supporting figure -->
          <figure
            class="relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
          >
            <img
              src="/images/guides/circle-pattern-black-white.webp"
              alt="Abstract circle pattern diagram suggesting structure and relationships"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover"
            />
            <figcaption class="sr-only">
              Visual: abstract structure map
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 - 3-question router -->
      <section id="router" class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          A simple way to decide
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-4">
          Three questions shape the right path. Answer them plainly and the
          platform and scope tend to follow.
        </p>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <ol
              class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
            >
              <li>
                Primary outcome: inquiries, portfolio trust, content visibility,
                or transactions.
              </li>
              <li>Update rhythm: rarely, monthly, or weekly.</li>
              <li>
                Ownership: DIY edits, light assistance, or set and forget.
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Typical mappings
            </h3>
            <ul
              class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
            >
              <li>
                Inquiries + rarely -> one-page or light multi-section site.
              </li>
              <li>Portfolio trust + monthly -> case-study site.</li>
              <li>
                Content + weekly -> content-led site with a simple editor.
              </li>
              <li>
                Transactions -> add modules or choose a platform with them built
                in.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 - Choose your path -->
      <section id="paths" class="mb-16 md:mb-20">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Choose your path
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
          These common patterns keep things focused. Start with one and expand
          only when the next step is clear.
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <!-- Consultant or coach -->
          <article
            class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
          >
            <div class="p-6">
              <h3
                class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
              >
                Consultant or coach
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                Plain services, clear outcomes, and a simple way to book. Add a
                few proof items and skip extras you will not maintain.
              </p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-2">
                Fit: Astro or lean WordPress. Visual builder if you want DIY
                layout changes.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Boutique studio -->
          <article
            class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
          >
            <div class="p-6">
              <h3
                class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
              >
                Boutique studio
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                Portfolio with short case studies and a simple approach page.
                Your taste and narrative carry the sale.
              </p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-2">
                Fit: Astro custom expression or WordPress if you will publish.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Local service -->
          <article
            class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
          >
            <div class="p-6">
              <h3
                class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
              >
                Local service
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                One simple page that answers what, where, proof, and contact.
                Accuracy and speed matter most.
              </p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-2">
                Fit: hosted suite or lean WordPress. Strengthen basic profiles.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-4">
          When unsure, start small. Expand as the site proves its value.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3b - Website needs by business type -->
      <section id="business-website-needs" class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Website needs by business type
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
          A quick comparison for context. Use it to sanity check the path you
          choose.
        </p>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Consultant or coach
            </h3>
            <ul
              class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1"
            >
              <li>Outcome: qualified inquiries and calls.</li>
              <li>Must-have: Home, Services, About, Proof, Contact or Book.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Boutique studio or agency
            </h3>
            <ul
              class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1"
            >
              <li>Outcome: portfolio trust and fit.</li>
              <li>Must-have: Home, Work or Case Studies, Approach, Contact.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Local service
            </h3>
            <ul
              class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1"
            >
              <li>Outcome: calls, directions, quick credibility.</li>
              <li>
                Must-have: one page or light multi-section with essentials.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2"
            >
              Restaurant or cafe
            </h3>
            <ul
              class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1"
            >
              <li>
                Outcome: menu views, reservation or order, hours and location.
              </li>
              <li>
                Must-have: Home, Menu, Hours and Location, Contact or Reserve.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 - Capabilities menu -->
      <section id="capabilities" class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          Capabilities menu
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-4">
          Think in capabilities, not brand names. We pick specific tools
          together and keep them minimal and durable.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 max-w-3xl">
          <ul
            class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
          >
            <li>Booking - a simple calendar to schedule calls or sessions.</li>
            <li>
              Forms - contact, inquiry, or light intake routed to your inbox.
            </li>
            <li>
              Email updates - occasional notes that compound trust over time.
            </li>
            <li>Proof - case studies, testimonials, galleries, and logos.</li>
            <li>
              Payments - straightforward checkout links or invoices as needed.
            </li>
            <li>
              Analytics - privacy-first basics to learn without heavy tracking.
            </li>
            <li>
              Search presence - clear titles, accurate profiles, tidy structure.
            </li>
            <li>
              Performance and accessibility - fast and readable by default.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5 - The art of your website -->
      <section
        id="art"
        class="mb-16 md:mb-24 rounded-xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6 md:p-10"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          The art of your website
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          Structure makes a site understandable. Expression makes it yours.
          Type, rhythm, spacing, color, and language create tone and trust. We
          keep it calm and credible while reflecting your taste.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6 - Thoughtful accelerators -->
      <section id="accelerators" class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          Thoughtful accelerators
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-3">
          A lightweight assist can speed thinking and reduce rework. We keep it
          practical and human-led.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Drafting help for sitemaps, outlines, and first-pass copy.</li>
          <li>
            Quick prototypes to test pacing and structure before we commit.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7 - How we might work -->
      <section id="process" class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          How we might work
        </h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-1.5"
            >
              Clarity session
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Map your path, define the smallest effective website, and choose a
              platform.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-1.5"
            >
              Design and build
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Small, fast Astro or WordPress sites that are considered and easy
              to live with.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
          >
            <h3
              class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-1.5"
            >
              Ongoing
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Light updates, new proof items, and tuning. Complex apps get a
              referral.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8 - Questions worth considering -->
      <section id="questions" class="mb-16 md:mb-20">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3"
        >
          Questions worth considering
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-3">
          Answer briefly, then pick your smallest effective site.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>What is the one action a first-time visitor should take?</li>
          <li>
            How will people find you and what proof will help them decide?
          </li>
          <li>How often will you update and who will own changes?</li>
          <li>What is your 90-day goal for the site?</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- What to do next -->
      <section
        id="next"
        class="pt-8 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
      >
        <div
          class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4"
        >
          <a
            href="/guides/planning"
            class="inline-block bg-blue-700 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-800 transition dark:bg-blue-500 dark:hover:bg-blue-400"
          >
            Open Planning
          </a>
          <a
            href="/guides/web-builders"
            class="inline-block border border-blue-700 text-blue-700 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-50 transition dark:border-blue-300 dark:text-blue-300 dark:hover:bg-blue-900/30"
          >
            Read Platform Overview
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-3">
          Prefer examples by business type? See the comparison above.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
